# Values the PII gate (tools/pii-gate.py) lets through. One per line:
#   <exact value> # <reason>
# The value is compared as written and case-folded. Every entry needs a reason;
# prefer an inline `pii-ok: <reason>` marker when the value is on one line only.

# Tool@host flag ids in network tests: the tool name and the host it reached.
npm@registry.npmjs.org # flag id tool@host, not a mailbox
curl@evil.io # flag id tool@host, not a mailbox
pip@pypi.org # flag id tool@host, not a mailbox

# Invented addresses in IOC and reputation tests. 6.6.6.6 is the IOC fixture;
# the others sit just outside a reserved range to test its boundary.
6.6.6.6 # invented IOC address
1.2.3.4 # placeholder address in a version-parsing test
172.32.0.1 # one past 172.16.0.0/12, boundary test
100.63.0.1 # one below 100.64.0.0/10, boundary test
100.128.0.1 # one above 100.64.0.0/10, boundary test
198.17.0.1 # one below 198.18.0.0/15, boundary test
198.20.0.1 # one above 198.18.0.0/15, boundary test
223.1.1.1 # public-range control value in a reputation test
192.0.1.1 # one below 192.0.2.0/24, boundary test
203.0.114.1 # one above 203.0.113.0/24, boundary test

/home/jane # "Jane Doe", the placeholder name, in a systemd unit test

# Windows known-folder GUID (FOLDERID_System), a Microsoft constant.
1AC14E77-02E7-4E5D-B744-2EB1AE5198B7 # Windows FOLDERID_System constant

# Documentation and fixture credentials, all fabricated.
AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE # AWS's own documentation key
vcp_notarealtokenjustafixture01 # self-describing fixture token
npm_config_registry # npm environment variable name, not a token
sk_live_00fictionalvalue0000 # demo-fleet fixture
ghp_0000fictionalpat00000000 # demo-fleet fixture
sk-ant-api03-0000fictionalkey0000 # demo-fleet fixture
password # the literal placeholder in scheme://user:password@host examples
06.06.06.06 # 6.6.6.6 written with leading zeros, IOC test
::ffff:606:606 # 6.6.6.6 as an IPv4-mapped IPv6 address, IOC test
08.1.1.1 # leading-zero host an IOC test feeds to the URL parser
